#: ../../source/accessibility.md:1 56eff416c57a4a8a9e08a8a4194654c4
msgid "Accessibility Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:3 6dcb815681cd46b7b5166e84e0eaa1ce
msgid ""
"`findfmt` is committed to providing an accessible, inclusive experience "
"for all users and contributors, regardless of ability or assistive "
"technology."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:6 b69218394bc64183a6052a14f0f6bbea
msgid ""
"We strive to align our command-line tools, documentation, and community "
"workflows with the [Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 Level"
" AA](https://www.w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/) standards "
"wherever applicable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:12 7a786bf637084dfbb76ed214f8736d53
msgid "1. Supported Environments & Assistive Technologies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:14 86c5f21652a3497b9ddc24b68cb191dd
msgid "1.1. Command-Line Interface (CLI)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:16 99c90ac261294cd0bbc52afff1f40c75
msgid ""
"The `findfmt` CLI is designed from the ground up for compatibility with "
"terminal screen readers and assistive tooling:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:19 811055d2840341439a281934a068de60
msgid ""
"**Screen Reader Compatibility**: Verified for predictable speech output "
"on standard terminal emulators across Linux "
"([Orca](https://help.gnome.org/orca/)), macOS "
"([VoiceOver](https://www.apple.com/accessibility/features/?vision)), and "
"Windows ([NVDA](https://www.nvaccess.org/) and [JAWS](https://vispero.com"
"/jaws-screen-reader-software/))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:23 77841978f3ac451c98612d9c616f6415
msgid ""
"**Stream-Oriented Plain Text**: CLI output emits linear, deterministic "
"text streams to `stdout` and error diagnostics to `stderr` without ANSI "
"escape codes, cursor jumps, or animated spinners in standard execution "
"modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:26 bbc5d9e120a14994a45d2e3235c45aee
msgid ""
"**Machine-Readable Delimiters**: Supports `-0` / `--print0` NUL-separated"
" streaming for unambiguous parsing and programmatic integration with "
"`xargs -0` and automated scripts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:28 c2ae7525303d48b08c4caa2ed6ba6b10
msgid ""
"**Color Independence, `NO_COLOR`, `FORCE_COLOR`, & `TERM=dumb` Support**:"
" No critical information is communicated exclusively through color. "
"`findfmt` honors explicit `--color` / `--no-color` flags first, followed "
"by [`NO_COLOR`](https://no-color.org/) (disabling ANSI styles whenever "
"`NO_COLOR` is non-empty), `FORCE_COLOR` / `CLICOLOR_FORCE`, `CLICOLOR=0`,"
" and `TERM=dumb` / `TERM=unknown`, and disables ANSI styling by default "
"whenever output is redirected to a non-TTY pipe or file unless enabled by"
" a higher-precedence setting such as `--color` or `FORCE_COLOR=1` "
"(`src/findfmt/cli/terminal.py`). Behavior is identical across both the "
"native Rust extension (`findfmt._rust_ext`) and pure-Python fallback "
"(`findfmt._fallback`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:35 bb58cb4152a84add8e82fbafae5f01bd
msgid ""
"**Localized, Sanitized Diagnostics Across Rust & Python**: Traversal I/O "
"warnings and CLI diagnostics coming from either `findfmt._rust_ext` or "
"`findfmt._fallback` are formatted through "
"`src/findfmt/cli/diagnostics.py`, translated via GNU `gettext` "
"(`findfmt.i18n`), and stripped of ANSI escape codes, C0/C1 control "
"characters, Unicode bidirectional (`BiDi`) overrides, and invalid UTF-8 "
"surrogates before reaching `stdout` or `stderr`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:39 6af1e45c3d944ecdb93a23c7f0ecd9f1
msgid "1.2. Project Documentation & Web Systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:41 47e60e4576f74ad68e2d8f3cdb80eb0e
msgid ""
"Our web documentation (hosted via Sphinx and GitHub Pages) is configured "
"to adhere to WCAG 2.1 Level AA standards:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:44 ad1aeabcbefe465c9baea3846454ead7
msgid ""
"**Semantic Markup**: Uses structured HTML landmarks (`<nav>`, `<main>`, "
"`<article>`, `<aside>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`) to facilitate smooth "
"screen reader orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:46 c7834cb262d44caeb13004823e678823
msgid ""
"**Clear Heading Hierarchy**: Maintains sequential heading levels (`H1` "
"through `H6`) to ensure reliable section jumping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:48 9f1810058b594736a359ebdfc622f0a4
msgid ""
"**Contrast Ratios**: Ensures text-to-background contrast ratios exceed "
"the 4.5:1 minimum threshold for normal body text and 3:1 for large "
"headings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:50 0daf3dee929e484a97639838913629dd
msgid ""
"**Keyboard Navigation**: All interactive elements (search modals, "
"navigation sidebars, code-copy buttons) are fully operable via keyboard "
"focus indicators without mouse interaction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:52 63db2e41926a4a65b9e9ae196c74f848
msgid ""
"**Descriptive Alt Text**: Graphical assets, diagrams, and illustrations "
"provide clear, contextual alternative text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:57 89686410659d45309b36458dd7d61204
msgid "2. Known Limitations & Workarounds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:59 4b0a3cf695f247dbb33f7279b25111d3
msgid ""
"While we actively work to identify and eliminate barriers, some external "
"environments may present constraints:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:61 7a2494c6962b4f2194ea87939ed8dfcc
msgid ""
"**Terminal Emulator Color Schemes**: Highly customized terminal themes "
"with non-standard contrast profiles may impact ANSI code readability. "
"**Workaround**: Set `export NO_COLOR=1` in your shell environment to "
"force monochrome output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:64 96a30bc6c183470086d0a2aa22a52aaf
msgid ""
"**Wide Delimited Streams**: When inspecting verbose file lists with long "
"absolute paths, terminal word-wrapping can impact speech cadence on "
"certain screen readers. **Workaround**: Use relative path traversal (the "
"default behavior) or pipe into a pager such as `less -R`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:70 f5b387b3e9b9442a902a850479bee454
msgid "3. Reporting Accessibility Barriers & Feedback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ACCESSIBILITY.md:72 ba7e9ef9ea764bda8208d16abc648600
msgid ""
"We actively welcome feedback and bug reports from users who encounter "
"barriers while interacting with `findfmt`."
msgstr ""

